1. Settlement Copilot (the AI part) — After your system settles offline payments, an AI reads PayPal's transaction records, compares them to your ledger, and says things like "these match" or "
₹300 is missing here, here's why." Like a smart accountant checking the books.

Use Cases in IRL:-Real situation	What the Copilot catches
🫖 Tea stall owner — 200 sales a day	"Only 199 reached PayPal. One got lost!"
📱 A phone glitch logged ₹150 instead of ₹100	"You think you earned ₹150, but you only got ₹100!"
⏰ A customer's token expired mid-sale	"This sale never finished — someone owes money!"
📅 Month-end taxes — a shopkeeper doing books	"Here's every rupee, already matched. No headache!"
🏪 Two branches of a shop	"Branch A is fine. Branch B keeps losing money to errors!"

2.Auto-invoices 
IRL Use:-
When a shop gets paid through your system, your code automatically emails them a PayPal bill and chases them if unpaid. No manual work.


3. Fraud + disputes — Someone later says "I never approved this payment." Your fraud service checks how risky it looks, then AI decides: refund the customer automatically, or fight it.


Future Implementations:-
4. Subscriptions — If Paron charges shops a monthly fee to use it, PayPal handles the recurring billing.
5. Dashboard — A screen showing PayPal's records side-by-side with yours, flagging differences.


